  <!-- ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
       § 06  OPEN QUESTIONS
       ────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="sh">
      <div class="sn">06 &nbsp; For the PM</div>
      <h2 class="st">Ten questions to answer before the coder runs.</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="body">
      <div class="gutter">Why</div>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          Each question has a sensible default. Confirming or overriding now
          prevents an awkward re-roll later. Full reasoning for each lives in
          <strong>01_pm_decision_brief.md</strong>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <ol class="qs">
      <li>
        <div>
          <h5>Track choice</h5>
          <p>L, M, or F? Picks how many prompts the coder runs.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="def"><b>Default</b>M</div>
      </li>
      <li>
        <div>
          <h5>Typeface flavor</h5>
          <p>Serif throughout (Economist register) or serif headlines + sans body (FT/Bloomberg register)?</p>
        </div>
        <div class="def"><b>Default</b>Serif throughout</div>
      </li>
      <li>
        <div>
          <h5>Accent</h5>
          <p>Single editorial amber on §-glyphs and drop caps, or pure monochrome?</p>
        </div>
        <div class="def"><b>Default</b>Amber</div>
      </li>
      <li>
        <div>
          <h5>Anchor-firms exhibit format</h5>
          <p>Bare list of four firms with one figure each, or tiny bar visualization? Bars risk implying cross-firm comparison the denominators don't support.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="def"><b>Default</b>Bare list</div>
      </li>
      <li>
        <div>
          <h5>What happens to the Core question pull-out</h5>
          <p>Drop, move next to ComparatorFrame, or move to the brief head?</p>
        </div>
        <div class="def"><b>Default</b>Move to brief</div>
      </li>
      <li>
